  {
   "where": "main/3/0",
   "type": "markdown",
   "value": "Why can a battery get thicker? Three simple reasons:\n\n1) **Breathing** When SoC goes up or down, the anode and cathode gently\nexpand and shrink (like lungs).\n2) **Irreversible swelling** Over life a thin **SEI “crust”** grows and\nadds permanent thickness (lower SoH → more swelling).\n3) **Compression** Squeezing the stack pushes back.\n- **Cylindrical**: the metal can fixes thickness; you can't tune the squeeze.\n- **Pouch/Prismatic**: you *can* clamp it (springs/pads). More squeeze = less empty space.\n\n### ⚙️ Knobs\n- **SoC** drives breathing\n- **SoH** lower = more SEI swelling\n- **Cylindrical** toggle fixed-thickness can\n- **Compression** clamp force for pouch/prismatic cells\n\n👉 Move the sliders and watch layers and total thickness respond.",
   "help": "",
   "key": null,
   "proto": {
    "body": "Why can a battery get thicker? Three simple reasons:\n\n1) **Breathing** When SoC goes up or down, the anode and cathode gently\nexpand and shrink (like lungs).\n2) **Irreversible swelling** Over life a thin **SEI “crust”** grows and\nadds permanent thickness (lower SoH → more swelling).\n3) **Compression** Squeezing the stack pushes back.\n- **Cylindrical**: the metal can fixes thickness; you can't tune the squeeze.\n- **Pouch/Prismatic**: you *can* clamp it (springs/pads). More squeeze = less empty space.\n\n### ⚙️ Knobs\n- **SoC** drives breathing\n- **SoH** lower = more SEI swelling\n- **Cylindrical** toggle fixed-thickness can\n- **Compression** clamp force for pouch/prismatic cells\n\n👉 Move the sliders and watch layers and total thickness respond.",
    "element_type": "NATIVE"
   }
  },
